# shell: desktop
# home: fixture
# CW-070/PVL-024: the desktop's own context menu arranges the DESKTOP.  The
# menu model is shared and rebuilt while windows draw, and the choice was
# handed to whichever window had focus -- so the items named things that
# never happened.
wait 8
note laid out by name, folders first: photos leads the row
expect-icon-screen photos 22 22
expect-icon-screen todo.txt 262 22
note the backdrop's own menu offers Arrange by, because the desktop is an
note icon view, and Icon size, because it is the desktop
press 700 500 3
wait 2
release 700 500 3
wait 5
expect-menu New folder|Arrange by|Icon size|Paste|Select…|Select all|Open parent|Add-ons|
note and reversing the order lays the DESKTOP out again in the other
note direction: what led the row now trails it
menu-pick Arrange by
wait 3
menu-pick Reverse order
wait 10
expect-icon-screen .Trash 22 22
expect-icon-screen photos 142 22
expect-icon-screen notes.txt 502 22
quit
